-- title:
--   Surjectivity criterion for local maps of complete local rings
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings, each local with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_R =$ `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R` and $\mathfrak m_S$ respectively, with $S$ Noetherian, and assume both are adically complete: $R$ is complete and Hausdorff for the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic filtration and $S$ for the $\mathfrak m_S$-adic filtration. Let $f\colon R \to S$ be a ring homomorphism subject to three hypotheses: (i) $f$ is local, i.e. $f(r) \in \mathfrak m_S$ for every $r \in \mathfrak m_R$; (ii) $f$ is surjective on residue fields in the elementwise form that for every $s \in S$ there is $r \in R$ with $s - f(r) \in \mathfrak m_S$; and (iii) $f$ is surjective on cotangent spaces in the form $\mathfrak m_S \le f(\mathfrak m_R)S + \mathfrak m_S^2$, where $f(\mathfrak m_R)S$ denotes the ideal `(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).map f` of $S$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_R$. The conclusion is that the underlying function of $f$ is surjective, so $f$ is a surjective ring homomorphism. The two rings are taken in the lowest universe.
--
--   This is the standard criterion, via Nakayama and successive approximation, for a local homomorphism of complete local rings with Noetherian target to be surjective once it is surjective on residue fields and on cotangent spaces; unlike the variants for finite algebras, no module-finiteness over $R$ is assumed. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd part of the development to produce surjections from power series rings and from the $uv$-crossing model onto rings prorepresenting deformation functors of special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_surjective_of_isAdicComplete_of_maximalIdeal_le_map_sup_sq.lean

